    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0261" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24210</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to my letter of June
                    18, 1920,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d188-f1"/> relative to the presence in Mexican
                    waters of a number of minor naval units sent there during the month of April of
                    this year, in obedience to a request of the Department of State, I have the
                    honor to say that the emergency having passed, I am of the opinion that these
                    units may now, with safety, be withdrawn from Mexican waters.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bainbridge Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
